A '''dust devil''' is a [[Slayer monster]] that requires level 65 Slayer to kill. They are located in the [[Smoke Dungeon]], the [[Catacombs of Kourend]], and the [[Wilderness Slayer Cave]]. A [[facemask]] (or a [[Slayer helmet]]/[[Slayer helmet (i)]]) must be equipped to fight dust devils effectively. Without a facemask, dust devils will always hit for 16 damage, fully drain the player's [[Attack]], [[Strength]], [[Ranged]], and [[Magic]] levels, and drain 50% of the player's [[Agility]], [[Defence]], and [[Prayer]] levels. With a facemask, dust devils attack with [[ranged melee|ranged-based melee]], meaning that high range defensive bonuses or the [[Protect from Melee]] prayer are effective protection against their attacks.

Dust devils cannot be assigned as a [[Slayer task]] until the [[mystical mirror]]s have been constructed during [[Desert Treasure I]].{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/Caveman_Only/status/914552814671671296|date=1 October 2017|archiveurl=https://archive.is/5cYCj|archivedate=27 May 2020|quote=I think all three of the checks you list are still in effect on the creatures in question. Reducing requirements tends not to be popular.}} Dust devils in the Catacombs of Kourend and the Smoke Dungeon are popularly killed by [[bursting]] (or [[barraging]]) and [[chinning]] while on-task.

Slaying a dust devil in the Smoke Dungeon with a Slayer helmet equipped is a requirement for the [[Hard Desert Diary]].

