*[[Smoke Dungeon]] - Entry into the Smoke Dungeon requires partial completion of [[Desert Treasure I]]. A [[facemask]] (or [[Slayer helmet]]) is required to counter not only the dust devils themselves, but also the dungeon's environmental effect, which can kill rapidly if unprotected. Dust devils can be found scattered throughout the western half of the dungeon, with a [[multicombat]] task-only area at the far end that has a much higher density of dust devils. A cannon cannot be used in the task-only area, though one ''can'' be used in the single-combat main dungeon area.

*[[Catacombs of Kourend]] - Dust devils can be found in the [[multicombat]] south-east section of the catacombs. These dust devils have more health and hit harder than those elsewhere. Ranged can easily be used to safespot across the water however the two north spawns can be lured to the western most arch and if the player stands under the eastern most tile under the arch, the two dust devils will remain semi-aggressive yet they can not damage the player despite being on the adjacent tile to the player nor will they run away. This allows for them to be hit with melee without the need for defence or prayer if lured with ranged damage. 

*[[Wilderness Slayer Cave]] - Dust devils can be found in the north-eastern quadrant of this [[multicombat]] dungeon, in a chamber just south of the [[greater demons]]. The dungeon entrance closest to the dust devils is in level 29 [[Wilderness]], while the devils themselves are in level 25-28 [[Wilderness]]. As with any other Wilderness location, be judicious about which pieces of equipment you are willing to risk losing to [[player killers]].

